1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Five synthetic teaching cases: two clean and three failures. They are excluded from release accuracy claims.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
n8n sends every execution through Pisama detection and idempotent retention.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The clean cases have empty mode sets. The timeout is independently labeled F13.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Expected and actual failure modes match exactly for all five teaching cases.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The repeat run is deduplicated, so n8n reruns cannot create duplicate retained executions.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Pisama immediately surfaces the synthetic failure findings for review.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The timeout evidence retains the 64-second duration, threshold, node, and F13 mode.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
A human marks the finding useful, completing the review step.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The synthetic teaching cases remain outside the verified 19-case release corpus.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Immutable run 2 scores 18 regression cases at 100 percent. The holdout stays excluded.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Every reviewed case exposes its append-only label history and evidence.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Corrections create new revisions, preserving earlier labels, hashes, and score records.
